      "side": 0,
      "message": "This logic changed to:\n```\n\tif ((jdata_ptr-\u003emagic !\u003d JUMP_DATA_MAGIC \u0026\u0026\n\t     !system_jumped_to_this_image()) ||\n\t    jdata_ptr-\u003eversion \u003c 1) {\n```\n\nThis fixes two bugs.\n1) JUMP_DATA_MAGIC signals that a jump occurred. It\u0027s zeroed early during system_pre_init to prevent unintentionally signaling that a jump occurred for the next image. So making this a criteria for valid jump data is inaccurate.\n2) This code should be forward compatible with future versions of the jump_data struct. Version 3 of the jump_data struct added a struct_size field. This field allows the move step below to work the same for any future version of the jump_data struct.\n\nWe could add a sanity check, e.g. version \u003c 100, to make this more robust against data corruption.",
